{"abstract":"UNLABELLED: The Purkinje fibers convey the electrical impulses at much higher speed than the working myocardial cells. Thus, the distribution of the Purkinje network is of paramount importance for the timing and coordination of ventricular activation. The Purkinje fibers are found in the subendocardium of all species of mammals, but some mammals also possess an intramural Purkinje fiber network that provides for relatively instantaneous, burst-like activation of the entire ventricular wall, and gives rise to an rS configuration in lead II of the ECG. AIM: To relate the topography of the horse heart and the distribution and histology of the conduction system to the pattern of ventricular activation as a mechanism for the unique electrical axis of the equine heart. METHODS: The morphology and distribution of the cardiac conduction system was determined by histochemistry. The electrical activity was measured using ECG in the Einthoven and orthogonal configuration. RESULTS: The long axis of the equine heart is close to vertical. Outside the nodal regions the conduction system consisted of Purkinje fibers connected by connexin 43 and long, slender parallel running transitional cells. The Purkinje fiber network extended deep into the ventricular walls. ECGs recorded in an orthogonal configuration revealed a mean electrical axis pointing in a cranial-to-left direction indicating ventricular activation in an apex-to-base direction. CONCLUSION: The direction of the mean electrical axis in the equine heart is determined by the architecture of the intramural Purkinje network, rather than being a reflection of ventricular mass.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Elbrønd (Bibs), Vibeke Sødring","Thomsen, Morten B.","Isaksen, Jonas L.","Lunde, Ester Danielsen","Vincenti, Stefano","Wang, Tobias","Tranum-Jensen, Jørgen","Calloe, Kirstine"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-666581"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Calloe, Kirstine"],"keyword":["ECG","Horse","Purkinje fiber","conduction system","mean electrical axis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intramural purkinje fibers facilitate rapid ventricular activation in the equine heart","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apha.13925","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-666581","identifier":[{"id":"85146457813","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36606541","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f43ab1ea-1cff-49d5-993f-bc6e66c2a708","ku-0610ed6d-dc8d-45cd-8436-454e366800d9"],"keyword":["ECG","Purkinje fiber","conduction system","horse","mean electrical axis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7870A37B85733453847714DADA7FA32D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apha.13925","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/401856153/Acta_Physiologica_-_2023_-_Elbr_nd_-_Intramural_Purkinje_fibers_facilitate_rapid_ventricular_activation_in_the_equine_heart.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346251188/Acta_Physiologica_2023_Elbr_nd_Intramural_Purkinje_fibers_facilitate_rapid_ventricular_activation_in_the_equine_heart.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Zoophysiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke Sødring","key":"elbrøndpau","last":"Elbrønd","locid":"1aeec376-9843-43e8-aea8-27ca67a85226","name":"Elbrønd (Bibs), Vibeke Sødring","name_org":"Elbrønd, Vibeke Sødring","orcid":"0000-0002-1588-5345","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten B","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"de1e0c60-60e1-46cb-b71c-32232c6ba6ed","name":"Thomsen, Morten B.","name_org":"Thomsen, Morten B","orcid":"0000-0002-2469-6458","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas L","key":"isaksenpau","last":"Isaksen","locid":"46a93bd5-94a8-4b64-b64f-e7cffd686aa7","name":"Isaksen, Jonas L.","name_org":"Isaksen, Jonas L","orcid":"0000-0003-3227-1131","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ester Danielsen","key":"lundepau","last":"Lunde","name":"Lunde, Ester Danielsen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefano","key":"vincentipau","last":"Vincenti","name":"Vincenti, Stefano","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7a3d91ab-5dbf-46e4-bc6e-634e16bd8d80","name":"Wang, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4350-3682","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"tranumjensenpau","last":"Tranum-Jensen","locid":"7f192af5-8907-4933-bfa7-41a462050a8f","name":"Tranum-Jensen, Jørgen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine","key":"calloepau","last":"Calloe","locid":"9fc39d74-d0ac-4774-b837-de97103c87f0","name":"Calloe, Kirstine","orcid":"0000-0002-1777-7938","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36606541"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apha.13925","issn":["17481708","17481716"],"issn_org":["17481708"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Physiologica","paperid":"e13925","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Acta Physiologica","volume":"237"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146457813"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f43ab1ea-1cff-49d5-993f-bc6e66c2a708","ku-0610ed6d-dc8d-45cd-8436-454e366800d9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Intramural Purkinje fibers facilitate rapid ventricular activation in the equine heart","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.93-666581","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
